+++ b/packages/core/src/arena/counters.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+// Water's beam answer (D1 4.2, docs/concepts/D1-combat-followup-and-progression.md sections 6.4-6.5). Tide Ward (mend II) is
+// the shape-class answer to a beam (mage-ai.ts), but a Water line plays one row per collar tier, so Tide Ward is gone by the
+// time the beams (Brand Wrath, Cyclone: tier IV) come, and the reference spends the mana and the mend line it would need.
+// Two PC-only rules, driven by the PC overlay (school-balance.pc.json `counters`):
+// - `tideWardHeld` (6.4 option A, the answer moves to a row Water has early): from tier III on, while an enemy beam runs, the
+//   mend line's slot plays Tide Ward, the row the line had at tier II (its own numbers, its own line cooldown).
+// - `tideWardBank` (6.5, the Water plan banks the answer): while Tide Ward can answer a beam build whose collar has opened its
+//   beam row, the Water AI keeps Tide Ward's mana and leaves the mend line's other rows alone (mage-ai.ts).
+// - `tideWardWindup` (6.6, the answer at the windup): the cue for Tide Ward is a rival beam's windup (its pending cast, a seen
+//   threat), not its channel. Once the mage's reaction delay has run from first sight of the windup, the Water AI presses a
+//   castable Tide Ward off its decision cadence; a beam it first sees in its channel does not cue the ward (mage-ai.ts).
+// Gate: a state that runs balance 'canonical' (CR-002/CR-007 parity) reads none of them, and all need an enemy build or beam,
+// so Water-only states (goldens, the default census) step exactly as before.
+// Imports stay leaf-ward (data, catalog, tuning, types) so water.ts and mage-ai.ts can read it.
